---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/schema';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What China Manufacturing Intelligence is, and what it is not."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>About {SITE_NAME}</h1>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is an independent, English-language editorial knowledge base for
      China\u2019s manufacturing geography.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-page">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      We document <strong>where things are actually made in China</strong>: the industrial
      clusters, anchor cities, specialized production towns, industries, and product
      categories that together form the world\u2019s largest manufacturing system.
    </p>
    <p>
      The product is not individual articles — it is a <strong>manufacturing knowledge
      graph</strong>. Every cluster, city, industry, and product page is a node, linked to the
      entities it depends on and supplies.
    </p>

    <h2>What this is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Not a sourcing blog or a \u201Ctop 10 factories\u201D list.</li>
      <li>Not a supplier directory — we do not rank or recommend individual manufacturers.</li>
      <li>Not promotional content for any company, region, or government body.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
    <p>
      Every factual claim is sourced and labeled. We never write from memory when
      verification is possible, never invent manufacturers, locations, production
      numbers, or certifications, and never convert a \u201Csupplier\u201D into a
      \u201Cmanufacturer\u201D without evidence. See the
      <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> for the full evidence hierarchy.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
